# Route a task (Codex)

Only on an explicit request, run the deterministic local router. It makes no model call and dispatches
nothing:

```bash
python3 {{REPO_DIR}}/router.py --explain "<the task>"
```

Present the selected profile, its confidence, the reasons, the alternatives, and
any clarifying questions the router returned. Ask the user before acting on a
new profile selection or new authority — recognition alone never grants either.
Do not use the router to repeat a question for a profile the user has already
authorized the parent to dispatch for the current task.

Planner and Builder are excluded from automatic recommendations and require
explicit role or PB invocation. For other profiles, once confirmed, load that profile's `agent-<key>` skill and adopt it. Never
auto-select a direct-call-only profile ({{DIRECT_CALL_ONLY}}); those run only on
an explicit request from the user.

The router never gives a worker authority to make a nested handoff. That remains
subject to the worker's `canDelegate`, `delegateTo`, and the task's authority.

Report what the router actually said. Do not infer a recommendation it did not
print, and do not substitute your own judgement for its output without saying
that is what you are doing.
